# Organizational Dimensions of Effective Digital Library Use: Closed Rational and Open Natural Systems Models.

**Authors:** Covi, Lisa, Kling, Rob

## Abstract
Describes a study of two research university libraries that examined digital library use of faculty researchers, librarians, and computer support providers in order to provide a theoretical model for understanding digital library use in different social worlds. Closed rational and open natural systems models in organizational theory are discussed. (Author/LRW)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ529666

